dpaa2_sec does not say how a compound frame (a job with m_dst: out of
place) came back from the SEC when it comes back as an event of the
crypto adapter: only the poll dequeue sets op->status, and an op of an
event stays RTE_CRYPTO_OP_STATUS_NOT_PROCESSED whether the SEC failed it
or not. bmchwaccel-engine (ticket 16 of .scratch/hw-accel-ls1088)
decrypts the ESP from the wire out of place, so as to send it up as it
came, and saw every job of it as failed. Set the status where the frame
is turned back into its op, for every way it comes back.

--- a/drivers/crypto/dpaa2_sec/dpaa2_sec_dpseci.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/dpaa2_sec/dpaa2_sec_dpseci.c
@@ -1723,6 +1723,12 @@
 	DPAA2_SEC_DP_DEBUG("%s", debug_str);
 #endif
 
+	/* what the SEC said, also for the events, which no dequeue reads */
+	if (unlikely(fd->simple.frc))
+		op->status = RTE_CRYPTO_OP_STATUS_ERROR;
+	else
+		op->status = RTE_CRYPTO_OP_STATUS_SUCCESS;
+
 	/* free the fle memory */
 	if (likely(rte_pktmbuf_is_contiguous(src))) {
 		rte_mempool_put(qp->fle_pool, (void *)(fle-1));
